{"G1146":{"id":"G1146","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1146","disambiguated_id":"G1146 =","unique_id":"G1146","headword":"δακτύλιος","transliteration":"daktulios","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"ring","definition_en":"δακτύλιος, -ου, ὁ\n (δάκτυλος), [in LXX chiefly for טַבַּעַת ;] \na ring: Luk.15:22.†\n (AS)","source_line":1278}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"anel","count":1}]},"G1544":{"id":"G1544","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1544","disambiguated_id":"G1544 =","unique_id":"G1544","headword":"ἐκβάλλω","transliteration":"ekballō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to expel","definition_en":"ἐκ-βάλλω \n [in LXX chiefly for גָּרַשׁ pi., also for שָׁלַךְ hi., יָצָא hi., יָרַשׁ hi., etc. ;] \n__1. to drive, cast or send out, to expel: with accusative of thing(s), mid. (σῖτον), before εἰς, Act.27:38; pass., Mat.15:17; with accusative of person(s), Mat.21:12, Mrk.11:15, al.; δαιμόνια, Mat.7:22, Mrk.1:34, al.; id. before ἐκ, Mrk.7:26; παρά, Mrk.16:9; ἐν, Mrk.3:22; (ἐν) τ. ὀνόματι, Mat.7:22, Mrk.9:38; λόγῳ, Mat.8:16; before ἔξω, Jhn.6:37; id. with genitive, Mrk.12:8, al.; of expulsion from home, Gal.4:30; from the Church, III Jn 10. \n __2. In LXX and NT (like Heb. יָצָא and Aram. הַנְפֵּק), to command or cause to depart: Mat.9:38, Mrk.1:12 (see Swete, in l.), ib. Mrk.1:43 5:40, Luk.10:2, Jas.2:25; τ. κρίσιν εἰς νῖκος (to cause to proceed to its goal), Mat.12:20 (LXX). \n __3. to reject (cl.): τ. ὄνομα ὑμῶς ὡς πονηρόν (cf. Deu.25:14), Luk.6:22; to leave out, Rev.11:2. \n __4. to take, draw or pluck out; \n __(a) with violence: Mat.7:5, Mrk.9:47, Luk.6:42; \n __(b) to bring forth or out of: Mat.12:35, Luk.10:35. \n (AS)","source_line":1684}],"occurrence_count":81,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"expulsa","count":11},{"gloss":"expulsar","count":7},{"gloss":"expulso","count":6},{"gloss":"tirar","count":4},{"gloss":"tira","count":4},{"gloss":"fora","count":4},{"gloss":"expulsaram","count":4},{"gloss"